---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { community, release } from "../data/release";
---

<Base
  title="Community — Pyrite"
  description={`${community.people} people have code in Pyrite ${release.version}. Here is who they are and how to join them.`}
>
  <section class="px-6 py-20 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Community</h1>
    <p class="text-text-secondary text-lg mb-6 leading-relaxed">
      When v{community.previousVersion} shipped in September, {community.outsideContributorsAtPrevious}
      people outside the maintainer had ever landed a change in Pyrite. By
      v{release.version}, {community.outsideContributors} have — {community.people}
      people in all, with {community.outsidePrs} of the {community.mergedPrs} pull
      requests ever merged coming from contributors, and {community.openPrsFromContributors}
      of the {community.openPrs} open right now.
    </p>
    <p class="text-text-secondary mb-12 leading-relaxed">
      Their work runs from documentation fixes to storage, search and MCP fixes
      and new test coverage. The 0.25 security releases carried contributor
      fixes alongside the maintainer's own.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Contributors</h2>
    <ul class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3 mb-4">
      {
        community.contributors.map((login) => (
          <li>
            <a
              href={`https://github.com/${login}`}
              class="block rounded-lg bg-surface-raised border border-line px-4 py-2 font-mono text-sm text-text-secondary hover:text-text-primary hover:border-white/20 transition-colors truncate"
            >
              @{login}
            </a>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <p class="text-text-muted text-sm mb-16">
      Plus the maintainer,
      <a href="https://github.com/markramm" class="underline hover:text-text-secondary"
        >@markramm</a
      >. Counted from GitHub's contributor list, commit authors and co-author
      credits, with anyone who commits under two names counted once. Missing
      from the list? Open an issue on this site's repo.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Join in</h2>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      <a
        href="https://github.com/pyrite-wiki/pyrite/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md"
        class="block p-6 rounded-xl bg-surface-raised border border-line hover:border-white/20 transition-colors"
      >
        <div class="font-semibold mb-2">Read CONTRIBUTING</div>
        <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Setup, tests, how changes are reviewed, and the changelog fragment
          every pull request carries.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/pyrite-wiki/pyrite/issues"
        class="block p-6 rounded-xl bg-surface-raised border border-line hover:border-white/20 transition-colors"
      >
        <div class="font-semibold mb-2">Pick up an issue</div>
        <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Bugs, docs that don't match the code, and roadmap work, all on GitHub.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/pyrite-wiki/pyrite/blob/main/SECURITY.md"
        class="block p-6 rounded-xl bg-surface-raised border border-line hover:border-white/20 transition-colors"
      >
        <div class="font-semibold mb-2">Report a vulnerability</div>
        <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Privately, through SECURITY.md. Multi-user hardening is where help
          matters most right now.
        </p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
